 6. **Overview** now shows MTTD / MTTR. **Audit trail** shows every step, including denied attempts.
 7. **Backup & restore**, **Detection rules**, **Security terminal** all demand the same QR + biometric step.
 
+## Accounts, authenticator enrolment and passwords
+- **Link an authenticator app:** sign in → **My account → Set up authenticator**, scan the QR, type the first 6-digit code. Works with
+  **Microsoft Authenticator** (use *+ → Other account (Google, Facebook, etc.)*, not "Work or school"), Google Authenticator, Authy, 1Password, Aegis or any TOTP app.
+  Turn on the app's fingerprint/face lock so the code needs your biometric. Once linked, the `demo-fingerprint` reference stops working for that account.
+  Replacing an authenticator needs your password *and* a current code. Codes are single-use (replay protected).
+- **Change password:** My account → Change password (needs the current password; signs out every other session).
+- **Forgot password:** *Forgot password?* on the sign-in page, using the authenticator code (throttled to 5 tries / 15 min).
+- **Admins (Users page):** edit email/role, deactivate/reactivate, reset a user's password (temporary password shown once; the user must change it
+  at next sign-in) and reset a user's authenticator after a lost phone. Role changes, deactivation and both resets need QR + authenticator verification
+  and are audited. You cannot demote/deactivate yourself or the last active administrator.
+- New users created by an admin must choose their own password at first sign-in. Set `BIOMETRIC_MODE=totp` to disable the demo reference entirely.
+- Existing databases are upgraded in place on start (new columns are added automatically).
+
